[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_plan")
title = "Open ground, 200 m"
question = "FRIENDLY FIRE AND TARGET CHURN, ON A REAL MAP INSTEAD OF THE ARENA. Two forces advance into each other from 200 m down the middle of the Coast Road, which is the longest open run in the repo — the sim arena is too small for any of this to show.

Three questions:

1. DO ROVERS SHOOT EACH OTHER? Four a side, same gun, advancing in formation. If machine guns spray through friends this is where it appears.

2. DO LOBBERS WASTE THEIR SHOTS? A grenade takes seconds to land, and a target picked because it is nearest is often dead before the round arrives. Watch friendly fire AND damage dealt per run: overkill looks like low damage for a long fight. The arena baseline already had Lobbers putting 18.8% of their damage into their own side, four times any other force.

3. WHAT IS NORMAL? Eight rifles a side is the control. Small arms hit instantly and have no blast, so whatever friendly fire they record is the floor that crossfire alone produces at this range.

Sides swap every other run so the road's own shape cannot favour one of them."
matchups = Array[Resource]([SubResource("M1_ROVERS"), SubResource("M2_LOBBERS"), SubResource("M3_RIFLES")])
level = ExtResource("7_coast")
site = Vector3(0, 0, 24)
site_heading = 90.0
repeats_override = 0
speed = 4.0
